{% endif %}RULES
1. instance.json carries the candidate exactly as you were given it. Never invent a URL or a
   commit hash.
2. Scripts must work on the blank machine: no paths into places only your machine has, no
   files outside bench/. Version directories have random names; your scripts receive them as
   arguments.
3. Later stages run the earlier checks again, so a change that breaks an earlier stage is
   reported at that earlier check.

Reply with ONE JSON object and nothing else, carrying ONE command; a reply that lists several
commands is refused, so three files take three replies. Escape quotes and newlines inside
JSON strings.
